      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Advances in coronary angiographic imaging have been recently realized with the advent of so-called flat panel technology. However, some of the limitations of coronary angiography, including the so-called pseudo-thrombus appearance of focal highly calcific coronary artery lesions remain. This case highlights the utility of intravascular ultrasound in determining the pathobiology of coronary artery lesions in select cases."},
